 "notes": "Observed 90% single-sided CL upper limit on g_agamma from Fig. 7 (top), extracted from the vector PDF img/Quax_LNF_2024_150.pdf in the arXiv e-print (blue filled exclusion region boundary; the violet curve is the expected limit and was not used). Axes calibrated from tick labels (linear mass in ueV, log10 coupling). Mass range 36.5241-36.5510 ueV matches the stated 36.52413-36.5511 ueV; curve minimum 9.07e-14 GeV^-1 agrees with the quoted best limit 0.882e-13 GeV^-1 within 3%. Paper assumes rho0 = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (stated in Fig. 7), matching the compilation convention, so no rescaling applied. Full vector-resolution curve (149 points) retained because the per-bin limit is spiky (adjacent points vary up to ~4x). The dark-photon recast (Fig. 8) was not used since g_agamma is the main result.",
